# The target builds a Stubble image per kernel, as the laptops' firmware
# provides no DTB: see dtb-loader.postinst.sh. Its kernel hook prefers
# systemd-boot-efi's systemd-stub to Stubble's own stub, so install that
# too. live-build adds their dependencies to the pool, and build-installer.sh
# reads this list for pkgsel to install them on the target. On trixie, stubble is only in trixie-backports (lb
# config --backports true in build-installer.sh). The 0100-dtb-loader binary hook
# also takes the AArch64 stubs from them.
#
#if DEBIAN_INSTALLER cdrom
stubble
systemd-boot-efi
#endif
